### How does communication work between services?

Synchronous REST or gRPC is used where an immediate answer is needed: creating a trip or getting a fare estimate. Asynchronous events over Kafka are used for everything high-volume or eventual: location pings, trip-state changes fanning out to notifications and analytics. Live trip tracking uses WebSocket.

```java
package com.bank.ridehailing.event;

public class TripStateChangedEvent {
    private String tripId;
    private String previousStatus;
    private String newStatus;
    private long timestamp;

    public TripStateChangedEvent(String tripId, String previousStatus,
                                  String newStatus) {
        this.tripId = tripId;
        this.previousStatus = previousStatus;
        this.newStatus = newStatus;
        this.timestamp = System.currentTimeMillis();
    }

    // Published to Kafka topic "trip-events"
    // Consumed by: notification-service, analytics-service, billing-service
}
```

### How do you handle security and monitoring?

Authentication uses tokens with scoped access. The API gateway validates every request, rate-limits, and terminates TLS. Service-to-service traffic uses mTLS. Authorization ensures a rider sees only their own trips. Payment details are encrypted and handled by the payment service alone.

```java
